<p>Ukrainian drone attacks hit targets in southern and northwestern Russia over the weekend, killing one person in Taganrog in the Rostov region and damaging homes and industrial sites there. Another strike sparked a fire at the Baltic port of Ust-Luga in the Leningrad region. Regional officials said emergency crews responded, moved evacuees out of affected areas, and later brought the Ust-Luga blaze under control. The attacks came as Ukraine has stepped up strikes on Russian infrastructure such as refineries, oil depots, and ports, which it says help fund Russia&#x27;s war effort. Ust-Luga is one of Russia&#x27;s largest petroleum export hubs, so the strike also highlighted how the war continues to reach deep into energy and logistics networks far from the front line.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/AVKXSw9qg33VpC5a6Hav8dQT34NKZ-tA5c-1n6vQaGbm34yEkexK_0NX0FQfwBEoVCc9Rc6Q2VMSwb_7S3RAABMPoOg6IdPZvPOiuy8DfhoH6deQfqvcArSzn8F_A8YzS30V1k4RSzTUUIC10ST-YAi6rx-0HRi9pecbnvbcxEcj1CTrYpFcdzu6I9SzxHCRg5L4GwmxkjTrprck1ijSoUuNvf5ga98LhkOmapDK-0AaCi-QZYNldUI' alt='Image published with coverage of the reported fire at Russia&#x27;s Ust-Luga port after a Ukrainian drone strike.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Energy corridor: Last week&#x27;s attacks on Ust-Luga and Primorsk set storage tanks on fire and forced a suspension of oil and oil-product loadings in Russia&#x27;s western export corridor.</li><li>Fire response: Authorities sent in extra firefighting resources from the Leningrad region and St Petersburg, including two fire trains, to contain the Ust-Luga blaze.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Rostov regional authorities: Governor Yuri Slyusar said one person was killed in Taganrog, civilians were evacuated from damaged areas, and emergency services were working at debris impact sites. (<a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/ukrainian-drones-kill-one-damage-homes-industry-southern-russias-taganrog-2026-03-29/'>Reuters</a>)</li><li>Ukraine: Ukraine has described its strikes on refineries, oil depots, and ports as justified retaliation aimed at reducing revenue that supports Russia&#x27;s offensive. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/russia-reports-fire-in-new-ukrainian-strike-on-major-baltic-port/article70800282.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Ukraine&#x27;s SBU security agency: The SBU said its long-range drones struck an oil terminal at Ust-Luga, causing serious damage and a fire at the port. (<a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/russias-ust-luga-port-damaged-by-more-ukrainian-drones/'>Michael West</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/ukrainian-drone-strike-in-southern-russias-taganrog/article70800846.ece'>Ukrainian drones kill one, damage homes, industry in southern Russia&#x27;s Taganrog</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/russia/636679-at-least-one-killed-in-russian-taganrog/'>At least one killed in Ukrainian attack on Russian city – governor</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/russias-ust-luga-port-damaged-by-more-ukrainian-drones/'>Russia’s Ust-Luga port damaged by more Ukrainian drones</a> - michaelwest.com.au</li><li><a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/ukrainian-drones-kill-one-damage-homes-industry-southern-russias-taganrog-2026-03-29/'>A person is killed by a Ukrainian drone attack in Taganrog, Rostov Oblast, Russia.</a> - reuters.com</li></ul>